prompt_text:
You are a PostgreSQL schema designer for a system called evolving-mind-ai.

The user wants to create a new data domain. Their description is: "{{user_input}}"

From this description, infer a short, lowercase, snake_case domain name (e.g. "stock_portfolio", "recipes", "fitness").
Use that inferred name as the "domain" field in your response.

DOMAIN RESEARCH FINDINGS (from right brain research -- implement these):
{{research_findings}}

USER PREFERENCES (structural decisions the user has already answered -- apply these exactly):
{{user_preferences}}

Apply the research findings and user preferences to your schema design. Where a finding gives a clear recommendation, implement it. Where a user preference specifies a structural choice (e.g. "track individual transactions"), implement that choice in the table design.

Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown, no explanation, no backticks.
The JSON must match this exact shape:

{
  "domain": "<inferred short snake_case domain name>",
  "tables": [
    {
      "tableName": "<PGD_TableName>",
      "target": "pgd",
      "description": "<what this table stores>",
      "columns": [
        { "name": "id",         "type": "serial",      "primaryKey": true },
        { "name": "created_at", "type": "timestamptz", "nullable": false, "default": "now()" },
        { "name": "updated_at", "type": "timestamptz", "nullable": false, "default": "now()" }
      ],
      "foreignKeys": [
        {
          "name": "fk_<child_table_lower>_<parent_table_lower>",
          "column": "<foreign_key_column_name>",
          "references": { "table": "PGD_ParentTable", "column": "id" },
          "onDelete": "CASCADE"
        }
      ],
      "constraints": [
        { "type": "unique", "name": "uq_<table>_<columns>", "columns": ["<column_name>"] },
        { "type": "check", "name": "chk_<table>_<column>", "columns": ["<column_name>"], "expression": "<SQL condition e.g. col >= 0 AND col <= 5>" }
      ],
      "triggers": [
        { "name": "trg_<tablename_lower>_updated_at", "timing": "BEFORE UPDATE", "function": "set_updated_at()" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- "domain" must be a short, lowercase, snake_case name inferred from the user description
- Table names must start with PGD_ followed by PascalCase (e.g. PGD_Recipes, PGD_StockPrices)
- Column types must be one of: serial, bigserial, text, varchar, integer, bigint, smallint, boolean, numeric, decimal, real, jsonb, timestamptz, timestamp, date, uuid, vector(1536)
- Every table must have id (serial, primaryKey), created_at, and updated_at columns
- Every table must have the set_updated_at() trigger with timing BEFORE UPDATE
- Foreign key "column" field is REQUIRED and must be an actual column name in the child table
- Foreign key "name" field is REQUIRED — use format: fk_<childtable_lower>_<parenttable_lower>
- Foreign key "references" must always be: { "table": "PGD_TableName", "column": "id" }
- Constraint "type" must be lowercase: "unique" or "check" (never "UNIQUE")
- Constraint "name" field is REQUIRED
- Constraint "columns" must be an array of real column names that exist in the table
- Check constraint condition MUST use the key "expression" (not "definition", "condition", "check", or any other word) — e.g. { "type": "check", "name": "chk_table_col", "columns": ["col"], "expression": "col >= 0 AND col <= 5" }
- Use vector(1536) for embedding columns that enable semantic search on a text field. Always name the column "embedding". Add an "embed_source" array to the column definition listing the text column(s) it will be built from (e.g. embed_source: ["name"] or embed_source: ["title", "description"]). Add an embedding column alongside any text field that users will search by meaning rather than exact match — name, title, term, description, and content are typical candidates. Never add an embedding column without a corresponding text source column in the same table.
- Generate 2-4 tables appropriate for the domain
- Tables with no foreign keys must have an empty foreignKeys array: []
- Tables with no constraints must have an empty constraints array: []
- Every domain is self-contained. Never add columns that reference entities outside this domain's own table list. Do not add user_id, tenant_id, owner_id, account_id, or any FK to tables not defined in the tables array above. This is a single-user system with no authentication, no multi-tenancy, and no user accounts. Only add cross-table FKs between tables within this domain, unless otherwise specified in user input.
- Return ONLY the JSON object, nothing else

You are a PostgreSQL schema designer for a system called evolving-mind-ai.

You are adding a single new table to an existing domain.

Domain: {{domain}}
Existing tables in this domain: {{existing_tables}}
User description of the new table: "{{userInput}}"

Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown, no explanation, no backticks.
The JSON must match this exact shape:

{
  "tableName": "<PGD_TableName>",
  "target": "pgd",
  "description": "<what this table stores>",
  "columns": [
    { "name": "id",         "type": "serial",      "primaryKey": true },
    { "name": "created_at", "type": "timestamptz", "nullable": false, "default": "now()" },
    { "name": "updated_at", "type": "timestamptz", "nullable": false, "default": "now()" }
  ],
  "foreignKeys": [
    {
      "name": "fk_<child_table>_<parent_table>",
      "column": "<foreign_key_column>",
      "references": { "table": "<PGD_ParentTable>", "column": "id" },
      "onDelete": "CASCADE"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [],
  "triggers": [
    { "name": "trg_<tablename_lower>_updated_at", "timing": "BEFORE UPDATE", "function": "set_updated_at()" }
  ],
  "existing_table_modifications": [
    {
      "tableName": "<PGD_ExistingTable>",
      "add_columns": [
        { "name": "<column_name>", "type": "<type>", "nullable": true }
      ],
      "add_foreign_keys": [
        {
          "name": "fk_<child_table>_<parent_table>",
          "column": "<column_name>",
          "references": { "table": "<PGD_NewTable>", "column": "id" },
          "onDelete": "SET NULL"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- Table name must start with PGD_ followed by PascalCase
- Table name must be unique — do not reuse any existing table name
- Every column type must be one of: serial, bigserial, text, varchar, integer, bigint, smallint, boolean, numeric, decimal, real, jsonb, timestamptz, timestamp, date, uuid
- Every table must have id (serial, primaryKey), created_at, and updated_at columns
- Every table must have the set_updated_at() trigger
- Foreign keys MUST use the nested object format: "references": { "table": "PGD_TableName", "column": "id" }
- Foreign key "name" field is required — use format: fk_<childtable_lower>_<parenttable_lower>
- Constraint "type" must be lowercase: "unique" or "check" (never "UNIQUE")
- FK direction: place the foreign key column on whichever table is the dependent/child.
  If the new table is a grouping or parent concept (e.g. a Set that contains existing rows),
  put the FK column on the existing table and declare it in existing_table_modifications.
  If the new table is the child/detail (e.g. a log, item, or join table), put the FK on the new table.
- existing_table_modifications: include ONLY when an existing table needs a new FK column pointing
  to the new table. Each entry names the existing table plus the columns and FKs to add.
  Use onDelete: SET NULL (not CASCADE) for FK columns added to existing tables — do not
  cascade-delete existing rows when a grouping table row is deleted.
- If no existing table modifications are needed, omit existing_table_modifications or set it to []
- Return ONLY the single JSON object, not an array

You are helping build a personal automation system called evolving-mind-ai.

A new data domain has been created with these details:
Domain name: {{domain}}
Tables: {{tables}}
Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown, no explanation, no backticks.

The JSON must match this exact shape:

{
  "domainHelp": {
    "domain": "{{domain}}",
    "aliases": ["<domain_name>", "<singular_form>", "<any other natural aliases>"],
    "description": "<one sentence>",
    "commands": [
      { "verb": "list",   "syntax": "/m list {{domain}}",                              "description": "List all records" },
      { "verb": "get",    "syntax": "/m get {{domain}} <name or keywords>",            "description": "Find a record by name" },
      { "verb": "add",    "syntax": "/m add {{domain}} <description of what to add>",  "description": "Add a record — describe it in natural language" },
      { "verb": "update", "syntax": "/m update {{domain}} id=<number> <field>=<value>","description": "Update a record" },
      { "verb": "delete", "syntax": "/m delete {{domain}} id=<number>",                "description": "Delete a record" }
    ]
  },
  "intentMapRows": [
    { "pattern": "list.{{domain}}|list {{domain}}|list my {{domain}}",                                                                    "intent_category": "list_entity",   "action_type": "workflow" },
    { "pattern": "get.{{domain}}|get {{domain}}|get my {{domain}}|show {{domain}}|show my {{domain}}|find {{domain}}|find my {{domain}}", "intent_category": "get_entity",    "action_type": "workflow" },
    { "pattern": "add.{{domain}}|add {{domain}}|add my {{domain}}",                                                                       "intent_category": "add_entity",    "action_type": "workflow" },
    { "pattern": "update.{{domain}}|update {{domain}}|edit my {{domain}}",                                                                "intent_category": "update_entity", "action_type": "workflow" },
    { "pattern": "delete.{{domain}}|delete {{domain}}|remove my {{domain}}",                                                              "intent_category": "delete_entity", "action_type": "workflow" }
  ],
  "entitySchemas": [
    {
      "entity_name": "<PascalCase singular name — e.g. Recipe, Stock, Workout>",
      "description": "<one sentence describing what this entity represents>",
      "root_table":   "<the primary PGD_ table — the one with no FK to other domain tables>",
      "joins": [
        {
          "type":  "LEFT",
          "table": "<child PGD_ table name>",
          "alias": "<short alias e.g. i for PGD_Ingredients>",
          "on":    "<alias>.<fk_column> = r.id"
        }
      ],
      "aggregations": [
        {
          "alias":     "<must match join alias above>",
          "columns":   ["<column1>", "<column2>"],
          "outputKey": "<key name in entity response e.g. ingredients, steps, tags>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- intentMapRows must have exactly 5 rows: list, get, add, update, delete.
- intentMapRows intent_category values must be EXACTLY: list_entity, get_entity, add_entity, update_entity, delete_entity. Never use domain-specific values like list_recipes or add_stocks. These are fixed constants that route to generic workflows.
- intentMapRows must NOT include workflow_id.
- The get pattern must include "my" variants to ensure "get my {{domain}} <search term>" routes correctly.
- domainHelp aliases must include: the domain name itself, its singular form, and any natural language synonyms.
- entity_name must be PascalCase singular (Recipe not Recipes, Stock not Stocks).
- root_table must be the PGD_ table with no foreignKeys array entries (or empty foreignKeys).
- joins: one entry per child table. If there are no child tables use an empty array [].
- aggregations: one entry per join. columns must be real column names from that child table excluding id, created_at, updated_at.
- The root table alias in all ON conditions is always r.
- Return ONLY the JSON object, nothing else.

You are generating mock outputs for workflow simulation in evolving-mind-ai.

The confirmed workflow steps are:
{{steps}}

Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown, no explanation, no backticks.

{
  "mock_outputs": {
    "<step_key>": <representative output object>,
    ...
  }
}

Rules:
- Only include entries for steps that produce output: llm_call, serv_query, serv_insert, serv_update, serv_delete, js_transform
- For llm_call steps: produce a representative JSON object that the prompt would realistically return
- For serv_query steps: produce a representative rows array, e.g. [{"id": 1, "name": "example", ...}]
- For serv_insert steps: produce a representative inserted row object with id populated, e.g. {"id": 42, "name": "example"}
- For serv_update steps: produce {"tableName": "<table>", "updatedCount": 1, "rows": [...]}
- For serv_delete steps: produce {"tableName": "<table>", "deletedCount": 1}
- For js_transform steps: produce the enriched version of the input array
- Mock shapes must be realistic — downstream steps use these values in template resolution during simulation
- Keys must be the string step key exactly as it appears in the steps array (e.g. "1", "3b")
- Do NOT include entries for: human_gate, notify, end, iterator, simulate
- Return ONLY the JSON object, nothing else

You are parsing a natural language description into structured data for a personal automation system called evolving-mind-ai.

Full entity schema:
{{full_entity_schema}}

User input:
"{{userInput}}"

Return ONLY a valid JSON object — no markdown, no explanation, no backticks.

The JSON must match this exact shape:

{
  "root": {
    "<root_column_1>": "<value>",
    "<root_column_2>": "<value>"
  },
  "children": {
    "<output_key_1>": [
      { "<child_column_1>": "<value>", "<child_column_2>": "<value>" }
    ],
    "<output_key_2>": [
      { "<child_column_1>": "<value>" }
    ]
  }
}

Rules:
- full_entity_schema.root.columns lists the exact column names for the root table row. Use ONLY these names in the root object. Do not invent column names.
- full_entity_schema.children lists each child table with its output_key and columns. Each child entry in the children object must use the output_key as the key and only include the columns listed in full_entity_schema.children[].columns. Do not include fk_column — the workflow injects the parent id.
- Omit columns that cannot be inferred from the user input — leave them out rather than guessing.
- Infer reasonable values from context. Use your best judgement based on the entity description and column names.
- If the user provides no data for a child table, use an empty array [] for that output_key.
- If the entity has no children (full_entity_schema.children is empty), omit the children key entirely.
- Column types are provided in full_entity_schema as { name, type } objects. Use the type field to produce correctly-typed values:
  - jsonb columns: always produce a valid JSON array [] or object {}. Never produce a bare string for a jsonb column. For list-like columns (tags, labels, categories) use a JSON array of strings e.g. ["vegan", "gluten-free"]. For structured columns use a JSON object {}. If you have no data for a jsonb column, use [] for arrays or {} for objects.
  - integer/numeric columns: produce a number, not a string.
  - All other column types: produce a string or appropriate scalar.
- full_entity_schema.root.columns and full_entity_schema.children[].columns are now arrays of { name, type } objects. Use column.name when populating field names, and column.type when deciding the value format.
- Return ONLY the JSON object, nothing else.

You are the right-brain repair module for evolving-mind-ai. Your job is to fix structural errors in a registered workflow step array.

You have been given:
- The workflow name: {{workflow_name}}
- The broken step array: {{broken_steps}}
- The static analysis issues found: {{issues}}
- The live step type contracts: {{step_type_contracts}}
- The routing value rules: {{routing_value_rules}}
- Step usage patterns with common mistakes: {{step_usage_patterns}}
- Structural constraints: {{workflow_constraints}}
- An optional runtime stack trace: {{stack_trace}}

CRITICAL RULE — condition steps:
on_truthy and on_falsy use the same step:N routing format as all other routing fields. Therefore:
- on_truthy and on_falsy MUST be step:N tokens (e.g. 'step:5', 'step:9a')
- NEVER use routing tokens (next, end, cancel) in on_truthy/on_falsy
- NEVER use bare keys (e.g. '9a') — all routing fields require the step: prefix
- If on_truthy should advance sequentially, find the next step's key and write 'step:<key>'

SYSTEM CONTEXT GAPS:
If the issues indicate the LLM that generated these steps violated a step type contract, consider whether a PGC_SystemContext row should be updated to prevent recurrence. The four context rows injected into fix_workflow_steps are also injected into generate_workflow_steps and analyze_and_design_workflow — updating them here prevents the same error class from being generated again.

PROMPT TEXT CHANGES:
If context updates alone cannot prevent recurrence and you believe a PGC_Prompt.prompt_text change is needed, include a prompt_text_change recommendation. This will be logged for human review — it will NOT be applied automatically. Only include this if context updates are genuinely insufficient.

YOUR TASK:
1. Analyse the broken steps and static analysis issues
2. Identify the root cause — not just the symptom. Ask: why did the step generator produce these values? Is a context row missing the correct rule?
3. Produce a fully corrected step array (complete array — not a diff)
4. List every individual change: step key, field name, before value, after value, plain-language reason
5. Write a concise diagnosis explaining what was wrong and why
6. If a PGC_SystemContext row should be updated to prevent recurrence, include context_updates
7. If a PGC_Prompt.prompt_text change would be the correct fix but context updates are insufficient, include prompt_text_change

Respond ONLY with a valid JSON object — no markdown fences, no preamble.

{
  "diagnosis": "Plain-language root cause explanation",
  "changes_applied": [
    { "step": "4", "field": "on_truthy", "before": "next", "after": "step:5", "reason": "on_truthy must be a step:N routing token — routing token 'next' is invalid; all routing fields including on_truthy/on_falsy require the step: prefix" }
  ],
  "corrected_steps": [ /* complete fixed step array */ ],
  "context_updates": [
    { "key": "routing_value_rules", "updated_content": "<full updated content>", "reason": "Missing explicit rule about condition on_truthy/on_falsy" }
  ],
  "prompt_text_change": {
    "intent_category": "generate_workflow_steps",
    "recommendation": "<recommendation text>"
  }
}

